=== Definitional Distinction from Fatigability

<subsec:fatigue-definition>

Fatigue in ME/CFS is most usefully defined as the *subjective* perception of exhaustion, reduced energy, and impaired motivation to sustain activity. It is formally distinct from *fatigability* — the *objective* decline in physical or cognitive performance during sustained effort. The two constructs correlate only partially and require different measurement approaches.

